    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2">
        <head>Af Rb 2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="16" ed="#liebermann"/>III. Be circena<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Rubrics-Af_2.lnote.oe.3"/> socnum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2" corresp="#wit-ot-frag"><pb n="16" ed="#liebermann"/>… ena socnum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2" corresp="#wit-g-prol"><pb n="16" ed="#liebermann"/>III. Be cyricena socnum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="17" ed="#liebermann"/>III. Be circena socnum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="17" ed="#liebermann"/>De confugio ad ecclesiam.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="186" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>III Be circena socnum</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="17" ed="#liebermann"/>Von Kirchen-Zufluchten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of sanctuaries in churches.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="187" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Concerning churches’ asylum</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">16</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyrec. <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> cyric. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyrec. So; cyric. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_2.lnote.de.0" n="0" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘Freiung der’ sondern ‘Aufsuchen von Kirchen’, ebenso Ine Rb 5. Quadr hatte das Richtige, ebenso Wilkins. Lambarde und Price folgend missverstand ‘Freiung’ Schmid, der aber 654a ‘Aufsuchen’ für möglich erklärt. Richtig jetzt Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> s. v. <hi rend="italic">ciricsocn</hi>. Die Bed. ‘Bezirk’ kommt für <hi rend="italic">socn</hi> vor Ende 10. Jhs. Agsä. nicht vor</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘sanctuary of’ but ‘seeking out of churches’; likewise Ine Rb 5. Quadr had the right sense, as did Wilkins. Following Lambarde and Price, Schmid misunderstood it as ‘sanctuary’, though at 654a he declares ‘seeking out’ possible. Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> s. v. <hi rend="italic">ciricsocn</hi> now has it right. The meaning ‘district’ does not occur for <hi rend="italic">socn</hi> in Anglo-Saxon before the end of the 10th cent.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
